turning now to the war in ukraine it is  day 100 of russia's war and ukraine's  president says that russian forces are  controlling 20 percent of the country an  area he describes as quote a complete  disaster ground and air assaults for  weeks have destroyed countless homes and  buildings throughout the eastern and  southern part of ukraine and thousands  of soldiers and civilians have been  killed in that bombardment mts taeyab  has this report on life in the russian  occupied city of harsan and we have to  warn you as we have so many times before  that these images may be hard to watch  hung by his wrists and put in stress  positions alexander guz a former  ukrainian military draftee says he was  tortured by russian soldiers and while  his scars are fading the memories of  what happened to him are not  they put a bag over my head and then  began beating me he says i was so  severely beaten i lost consciousness  kremlin black forces seized control of  his southern ukrainian hometown of  kursan in the early days of its invasion  since then moscow's grip on the city of  nearly 300 thousand has only tightened  with curson now an oppressive dystopia  where allegations of torture and  disappearances are widespread  through an encrypted video call we  connected with bogdan andrenko a  20-year-old volunteer providing aid to  people in need in croissant  you feel constantly under threat that  russians will come and take you away he  says a bunch of volunteers in the city  were already taken by the russians and  we don't know what happened to them you  must be at least a little bit afraid  that something might happen to you  every single day he says  [Music]  every so often video emerges from  croissant of ukrainian civilians  resisting russia's occupation  only to be met with violence those who  manage to make it out take shelter in  cities like odessa to the south where  they receive aid and other support  it's here we met olia chumachenko and  her four-year-old son kasia who fled  croissant over a month ago  i knew i had to leave the town i was  born in she says but i did it for my son  he's my only reason for living she says  now we have an update for you on those  long-range rocket systems that the  president authorized for ukraine this  week ukrainian forces are now in an  unspecified european country receiving  training on the weapons in the hopes  they can take back that territory from  russia gail  all right mts triumph in ukraine thank  you very much
 

